  "details": "- Name of the VRCSDK package you have imported.\nVRCSDK3-2019.12.19.19.56.unitypackage\n- Name of the Udon SDK package you have imported.\nUDONSDK-2019.12.19.18.37_Public.unitypackage\n- Version/build of VRChat you’re using to test, if necessary.\nIt's tested in Editor\n- A general description of the bug you’re encountering.\n- Step by step guide how to replicate the bug.\nI made a simple clock controller that's gets DateTime Now and splits it into 6 digits, set these digits to another Udon programs as int variables. References to other udons provided via public variables.\nIt's basicaly works as expected, but, for testing, consistency and optimization purposes, I want to cache DateTime into variable and re-use it immediately, so I am not going to use new copy of DateTime when computing these digits values. So I declaring new variable tmp_time of type DateTime and setting it at beginning ( https://i.imgur.com/10QvXhH.png ), then using get variable to access instance of DateTime ( https://i.imgur.com/UpdeXTT.png ). So, previous version of this Udon program only had \"DateTime Now\" instead of \"get variable tmp_time\", that's all the difference.\nThis program should work fine, however, it raises VRC.Udon.VM.UdonVMException: \nFull error text: https://gist.github.com/kawashirov/c51f21f05ffb951af8316fbe9d3cd355\nException Message:\n  An exception occurred during EXTERN to 'VRCUdonCommonInterfacesIUdonEventReceiver.__SetProgramVariable__SystemString_SystemObject__SystemVoid'.\n  Cannot retrieve heap variable of type 'DateTime' as type 'IUdonEventReceiver'\nAs you can see, for some reason Udon sends this instance of DateTime instead of UdonBehaviour into SetProgramVariable\nIn node graph everything is linked fine and types detected properly: \nhttps://i.imgur.com/K2pSRCi.png , https://i.imgur.com/MUBNuPF.png , https://i.imgur.com/p0ME30N.png\nFull udon grpah: https://gist.github.com/kawashirov/19da300a8442b798ce220e3afc37f923#file-graph\nFull asm text: https://gist.github.com/kawashirov/19da300a8442b798ce220e3afc37f923#file-asm\nThere is debug nodes on the right side, but it is not connected. It doesn't seems to affect anything and can be removed w/o any cahnges.",
